{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"a29d5859530e551c9c63051e6b73ecbf9e195803"},"timestamp":1576776374,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NzU4NDQ2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3950#issuecomment-567584466"},"message":"Some more strange behavior. At first the added sibling seems not configures (note questionamrk) than it is configured just by running the command with no specs:\n\n```\n[dorian@mri freesurfer]$ datalad siblings\n.: here(+) [git]\n.: origin(+) [/DATA/FEDERATED_DATASETS/STUDY1/data/processed/freesurfer (git)]\n.: mandy(?) [/DATA/dass/NewProcess/FEDERATED_DATASETS/STUDY1/data/processed/freesurfer/ (git)]\n[dorian@mri freesurfer]$ datalad siblings configure\n[ERROR  ] need sibling `name` for configuration [configure-sibling(/DATA/dorian/dataladtest/mergetest/FEDERATED_DATASETS/STUDY1/data/processed/freesurfer)]\n[dorian@mri freesurfer]$ datalad siblings configure --name mandy\n.: mandy(+) [/DATA/dass/NewProcess/FEDERATED_DATASETS/STUDY1/data/processed/freesurfer/ (git)]\n[dorian@mri freesurfer]$ datalad siblings\n.: here(+) [git]\n.: origin(+) [/DATA/FEDERATED_DATASETS/STUDY1/data/processed/freesurfer (git)]\n.: mandy(+) [/DATA/dass/NewProcess/FEDERATED_DATASETS/STUDY1/data/processed/freesurfer/ (git)]\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576803222,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2Nzc0MTY5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3950#issuecomment-567741696"},"message":"Thanks for the report.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003escript that triggers the issue\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\n\nset -eu\n\ncd \"$(mktemp -d --tmpdir dl-XXXXXXX)\"\ndatalad create source\ndatalad create super\n\ncd super\ndatalad install -d . -s ../source clone\n\ncd clone\ndatalad siblings add --name foo0 --inherit --url /tmp/dl-3950-qAnloP5/source\n```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\nIt looks like the issue is that, when inheriting settings from the superdataset, siblings._configure_remote() incorrectly assumes that a remote with the same name exists.  Something along the lines of the patch below should fix it.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/datalad/distribution/siblings.py b/datalad/distribution/siblings.py\nindex 26e93d73e..d17ced411 100644\n--- a/datalad/distribution/siblings.py\n+++ b/datalad/distribution/siblings.py\n@@ -468,7 +468,8 @@ def _configure_remote(\n             # makes sense only if current AND super are annexes, so it is\n             # kinda a boomer, since then forbids having a super a pure git\n             if isinstance(ds.repo, AnnexRepo) and \\\n-                    isinstance(delayed_super.repo, AnnexRepo):\n+                    isinstance(delayed_super.repo, AnnexRepo) and \\\n+                    name in delayed_super.repo.get_remotes():\n                 if annex_wanted is None:\n                     annex_wanted = _inherit_annex_var(\n                         delayed_super, name, 'wanted')\n```\n\nI'll plan to roll that into a proper patch tomorrow.  This area seems to lack dedicated tests of inheriting when the remote _does_ exist, so those should be added too.\n\n---\n\nI haven't looked into your second comment.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576803230,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI4OTkyMTEyMjM="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576881109,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5MDIyMjI0MTY="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576907034,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjkwMjUyMzgwMQ=="},"status":2}]}